WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.077
The serving runtime turns model files and accelerator resources into a network service.

00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:05.727
Llama.

00:00:05.727 --> 00:00:11.469
cpp server is portable and effective for quantized models across CPU and several GPU backends.

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:14.915
Ollama packages model management behind a straightforward local service.

00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:19.509
These tools are useful for labs and modest deployments where operational simplicity

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:21.806
matters more than maximizing concurrent throughput.

00:00:21.806 --> 00:00:26.400
VLLM is designed for high-throughput language-model serving and includes memory-management and batching

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.463
techniques suited to concurrent requests on supported hardware.

00:00:29.463 --> 00:00:31.760
Text Generation Inference, often called TGI,

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.205
is another production-oriented server with model-serving and observability features.

00:00:35.205 --> 00:00:39.799
Their advantages appear only when models, accelerators, and traffic patterns are compatible.

00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:42.479
Benchmark the actual model and prompt distribution;

00:00:42.479 --> 00:00:47.839
do not select a runtime solely from an impressive result produced on different hardware.

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:51.667
An OpenAI-compatible API can decouple clients from the underlying server.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:57.410
Applications use a familiar request format while a gateway or router directs traffic to llama.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.707
cpp, Ollama, VLLM, or another backend.

00:00:59.707 --> 00:01:03.918
Compatibility is not always identical across parameters, streaming, tool calls, embeddings,

00:01:03.918 --> 00:01:08.129
and error behavior, so test the features your clients depend on.

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:11.575
Open WebUI can provide a shared browser front end,

00:01:11.575 --> 00:01:16.551
but it should use the same authentication and routing controls as other clients.

00:01:16.551 --> 00:01:19.997
Introduce model routing only after one server is reliable.

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:23.825
Start a known model, confirm acceleration, measure latency and throughput,

00:01:23.825 --> 00:01:26.888
exercise health checks, and document startup and shutdown.

00:01:26.888 --> 00:01:30.333
Then replicate the service or add another model role.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:33.396
Complex orchestration cannot repair an unstable serving process;

00:01:33.396 --> 00:01:35.310
it only distributes the instability.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:40.020
A simple, observable serving layer is the foundation for safe scheduling and scale.
